{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/pulls/3306","id":3827228838,"node_id":"PR_kwDOEFLz887kHuCm","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/3306","diff_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/3306.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/3306.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/3306","number":3306,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"noise: re-delegate SSH check when the auth session is missing","user":{"login":"kloba","id":19997552,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5OTk3NTUy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19997552?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kloba","html_url":"https://github.com/kloba","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kloba/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kloba/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kloba/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kloba/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kloba/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kloba/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kloba/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kloba/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kloba/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What & why\n\n`/machine/ssh/action/{src}/to/{dst}` stores a pending SSH-check auth session in an in-memory, bounded LRU keyed by `auth_id`. The follow-up poll looks it up and, when it is missing, returns `400 \"no auth session found\"` (`ErrNoAuthSession`). The polling client (tailscaled) keeps retrying the **same** now-defunct `auth_id`, so the SSH connection hangs and eventually times out with no shell.\n\nThe session can be absent for ordinary reasons:\n\n- it was evicted from the bounded cache,\n- it expired (`register_cache_expiration`, default 15m), or\n- the control plane restarted (the cache is in-memory and not persisted).\n\nThe client cannot recover on its own — the only escape today is the SSH timeout. This is the failure mode reported in #3305.\n\nThe create → follow-up happy path is otherwise correct: the added `TestSSHActionHoldAndDelegate_PersistsAuthSession` drives the initial poll and asserts the session persists, and it passes without any behavioural change. The problem is solely the unrecoverable follow-up once the session is gone.\n\n## Change\n\nIn `sshActionFollowUp`, on a cache miss:\n\n- if the `(src, dst)` pair is still subject to an SSH check (`checkFound`) → restart the flow with a fresh `HoldAndDelegate` so the check can complete;\n- otherwise → keep returning `ErrNoAuthSession` (a genuinely bogus `auth_id`).\n\nGating on `checkFound` keeps re-delegation limited to pairs the policy actually wants checked; the dst machine-key check upstream already ensures only the real destination node reaches this path.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `TestSSHActionFollowUp_ReDelegatesWhenSessionMissing` — missing session + active check ⇒ `HoldAndDelegate`; missing session + no check ⇒ `ErrNoAuthSession`.\n- `TestSSHActionHoldAndDelegate_PersistsAuthSession` — happy-path regression guard.\n- Existing SSH action tests pass; `gofmt` and `go vet` are clean.\n\nAddresses #3305.\n\n---\n\n- [x] have read the [CONTRIBUTING.md](./CONTRIBUTING.md) file\n- [x] raised a GitHub issue (#3305) beforehand\n- [x] added unit tests\n- [ ] added integration tests\n- [ ] updated documentation if needed\n- [x] updated CHANGELOG.md\n","created_at":"2026-06-08T22:27:00Z","updated_at":"2026-06-10T09:48:03Z","closed_at":"2026-06-10T09:48:03Z","merged_at":"2026-06-10T09:48:03Z","merge_commit_sha":"71a4ce3c9fa12b9cb440392c0e9325c5a20950b5","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[{"login":"nblock","id":131119,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzMTExOQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/131119?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock"